From 73e8519f774778ddda172f308031b3cedf12c02b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Chen <119898205+sacchen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 15:08:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Fix crash when re-rendering an interrupted ParametricSurface

An exception escaping the face-construction phase of
ParametricSurface.triangulate() -- KeyboardInterrupt raised by
sig_check() when the user presses Ctrl-C, or an error raised by a
user-supplied color function -- left the object with fcount = m*n but
uninitialized face.vertices pointers.  The next render then hit the
"already triangulated" short-circuit and walked the half-built mesh,
crashing the interpreter (SIGSEGV/SIGBUS) in
IndexFaceSet._separate_creases.

Extend the guard that already covers realloc()/eval_grid() to the whole
triangulation, so any failure resets fcount/vcount and the next
triangulate() rebuilds from scratch.  Unlike the old guard, do not clear
render_grid: for surfaces defined by a function it doubles as the domain
that get_grid() returns, so clearing it left the object permanently
unrenderable (NotImplementedError from get_grid on every retry) -- a
second, pre-existing bug, reachable by interrupting eval_grid().

Add a doctest reproducing the corruption via a failing color function,
which raises inside the same face-construction loop as sig_check().

Fixes #2699

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
